045417] [17592186393562 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393562 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d5663d4b-636b-5cde-93d7-c48645e55519" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399538 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399538 #edb/ref 1069 "q-106775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399538 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399538 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine if $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nIf so, then what is the corresponding eigenvalue?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "56a4f3a9-ccca-53d2-8026-09ec5330fdbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399538 #edb/ref 1074 "The eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $v$ is an eigenvector, then there must exist a real number $\\lambda $ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ Hence, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]=\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis leads to the following system of equations for $\\lambda :$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}16=2\\lambda  \\\\ -8=-4\\lambda \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis system has no solution. Therefore, $v$ is not an eigenvector of $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399539 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399539 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #e